
# lean-ctx — Context Engineering Layer

PREFER lean-ctx MCP tools over native equivalents for token savings:

| PREFER | OVER | Why |
|--------|------|-----|
| `ctx_read(path)` | `Read` | Cached, 10 compression modes |
| `ctx_shell(command)` | `Shell` | Pattern compression |
| `ctx_search(pattern, path)` | `Grep` | Compact results |
| `ctx_tree(path, depth)` | `ls` / `find` | Directory maps |
| `ctx_edit(path, old_string, new_string)` | `Edit` (when Read unavailable) | Search-and-replace without native Read |

### Edit Fallback Rule (single source of truth)

1. Prefer **native `Edit` / `StrReplace`** when available.
2. If native `Edit` requires a prior `Read` **and** `Read` is unavailable → use **`ctx_edit`**.
3. **NEVER** loop on `Edit` failures. On the **first** failure, switch to `ctx_edit` immediately.
4. **Write, Delete, Glob** — use normally (no lean-ctx override needed).

---

## 🧠 Advanced Enhancement Integration

When working with files under `src/enhancements/` or interacting with the Green Agent's advanced modules, use the **enhanced read modes** available in lean-ctx to fetch only the most relevant state without reading entire files. This saves tokens and keeps context focused.

### Mode Taxonomy

```
Standard modes  ──►  full | compressed | outline | ...
Enhanced modes  ──►  graph | modp | rlhf | distillation | evolutionary |
                     moe | flexgen | cache | cost | workload | zero_trust |
                     routing | anomaly | safety | privacy | checkpoint |
                     training | experiment | digest
Composite modes ──►  mode="modp+moe" | mode="graph+routing" | mode="cost+energy"
```

### Enhanced Read Modes (standard set)

| Mode | Purpose | Example Module |
|------|---------|----------------|
| `graph` | LIMIT Graph metrics (centrality, connectivity) | `core/graph_registry.py`, `core/causal_graph.py` |
| `modp` | MODP weights and composite score | `schemas/node_descriptor.py`, `schemas/workload_descriptor.py` |
| `rlhf` | Human feedback score | `schemas/feedback_event.py`, `zero_trust_architecture.py` |
| `distillation` | Student stats, replay buffer size, MoE gate weights | `schemas/node_descriptor.py` (distillation optimizers) |
| `evolutionary` | Best fitness and population parameters | `schemas/node_descriptor.py` (evolutionary optimizers) |
| `moe` | MoE gating network weights and expert routing stats | `schemas/node_descriptor.py`, `schemas/workload_descriptor.py` |
| `flexgen` | FlexGen configuration, precision, energy metrics | `config/green_agent_config.yaml`, runtime logs |

### Enhanced Read Modes (extended set — new)

| Mode | Purpose | Example Module | Token class |
|------|---------|----------------|-------------|
| `cache` | Cache hit/miss stats, compression-mode histogram, eviction counts | `core/cache_manager.py` | tiny |
| `cost` | Composite cost: accuracy / energy / latency / carbon trade-off vector | `schemas/node_descriptor.py` | small |
| `energy` | Energy-only slice of `flexgen` (kWh, avg watts, p95) | runtime telemetry logs | tiny |
| `workload` | WorkloadDescriptor: SLO class, batch size, priority, tenant | `schemas/workload_descriptor.py` | small |
| `zero_trust` | Trust score, attestation state, policy decisions | `zero_trust_architecture.py` | small |
| `routing` | LIMIT graph routing decisions + next-hop probabilities | `core/graph_registry.py` | small |
| `anomaly` | Anomaly flags, drift scores, alert severity | `core/anomaly_detector.py` | tiny |
| `safety` | Guardrail state, blocked-policy counts, redaction stats | `core/safety.py` | tiny |
| `privacy` | DP ε/δ budget consumption, clipping norms | `core/privacy.py` | tiny |
| `checkpoint` | Last checkpoint id, step, loss, age | `training/checkpoints.py` | tiny |
| `training` | Combined `distillation` + `evolutionary` snapshot (composite) | `schemas/node_descriptor.py` | small |
| `experiment` | A/B test arm assignment, p-value, lift | `experiments/registry.py` | tiny |
| `digest` | One-shot human-readable digest of *all* enabled enhanced modes | (composite) | medium |

### Composite Modes (new)

`mode` accepts `+`-joined unions. Composite reads issue a **single** MCP round-trip and merge the result object.

| Composite | Equivalent | When to use |
|-----------|------------|-------------|
| `modp+moe` | MODP score **and** MoE gate weights | Trade-off **and** routing decisions together |
| `graph+routing` | Topology **and** next-hop probabilities | Explain *why* a route was chosen |
| `cost+energy` | Cost vector **and** raw energy | Carbon/latency debugging |
| `modp+rlhf` | MODP **and** feedback score | Policy adjustment review |
| `training` | `distillation+evolutionary` | Convergence monitoring |
| `digest` | All enabled modes | Onboarding, incident triage, "state of the world" |

### Usage Examples

```python
# --- core enhanced modes ---
ctx_read("src/enhancements/core/graph_registry.py", mode="graph")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/node_descriptor.py", mode="modp")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/feedback_event.py", mode="rlhf")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/node_descriptor.py", mode="distillation")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/node_descriptor.py", mode="evolutionary")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/workload_descriptor.py", mode="moe")
ctx_read("config/green_agent_config.yaml", mode="flexgen")

# --- extended modes ---
ctx_read("src/enhancements/core/cache_manager.py", mode="cache")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/node_descriptor.py", mode="cost")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/workload_descriptor.py", mode="workload")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/zero_trust_architecture.py", mode="zero_trust")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/core/graph_registry.py", mode="routing")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/core/anomaly_detector.py", mode="anomaly")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/core/safety.py", mode="safety")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/core/privacy.py", mode="privacy")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/training/checkpoints.py", mode="checkpoint")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/experiments/registry.py", mode="experiment")

# --- composite modes (single round-trip) ---
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/node_descriptor.py", mode="modp+moe")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/core/graph_registry.py", mode="graph+routing")
ctx_read("src/enhancements/schemas/node_descriptor.py", mode="cost+energy")

# --- one-shot state digest ---
ctx_read("src/enhancements/", mode="digest")
```

### Mode Selection Decision Tree

```
Need to EDIT a file?
├── yes → use full (or standard) mode  ── do not use enhanced modes
└── no  → need a single fact?
         ├── routing / topology      → graph | routing | graph+routing
         ├── trade-off / score       → modp | modp+moe | modp+rlhf
         ├── cost / carbon / energy  → cost | energy | cost+energy
         ├── model training state    → distillation | evolutionary | training
         ├── routing weights         → moe
         ├── inference delegation    → flexgen
         ├── security / trust        → zero_trust | safety
         ├── privacy budget          → privacy
         ├── cache health            → cache
         ├── anomaly / drift         → anomaly
         ├── workload / SLO          → workload
         ├── experiment state        → experiment
         └── "everything at once"    → digest
```

### When to Use Enhanced Modes

- **LIMIT Graph / Routing** — topology context for routing or anomaly analysis; use `routing` for next-hop probabilities.
- **MODP** — trade-offs between accuracy, energy, latency, and carbon.
- **RLHF** — when human feedback influences policy adjustments or routing priorities.
- **Distillation** — when checking if the student policy is learning or the replay buffer is filling.
- **Evolutionary** — when monitoring whether evolutionary optimisation is converging or stalled.
- **MoE** — when diagnosing expert routing stability or gate weight changes.
- **FlexGen / Energy** — when deciding to delegate LLM inference and checking energy consumption.
- **Cache** — when verifying that lean-ctx itself is delivering token savings.
- **Zero-Trust / Safety / Privacy** — when auditing security posture, guardrail blocks, or DP budget.
- **Checkpoint / Training / Experiment** — when tracking model lifecycle and A/B outcomes.
- **Digest** — for onboarding, incident triage, or a full state snapshot in one call.

### Token Budget Guidance (approximate)

| Mode | Tokens | Use when |
|------|--------|----------|
| `cache`, `anomaly`, `safety`, `privacy`, `checkpoint`, `experiment` | < 100 | quick health checks |
| `energy`, `routing`, `workload` | ~100–250 | targeted diagnosis |
| `modp`, `rlhf`, `zero_trust`, `moe` | ~250–500 | decision input |
| `graph`, `distillation`, `evolutionary` | ~500–1 000 | analysis |
| `flexgen`, `cost` | ~500–1 500 | configuration review |
| `digest`, `training` | ~1 000–3 000 | snapshot / triage |
| `full` | file-size dependent | **only when editing** |

### Configuration Matrix

Enhanced modes require the corresponding module to be enabled. If a flag is missing, the mode **silently falls back** to standard read (or empty result) and increments `lean_ctx.fallback.count{mode=...}`.

| Mode(s) | Enable flag |
|---------|-------------|
| all enhanced | `ENHANCEMENTS_ENABLED=true` |
| `graph`, `routing`, `anomaly` | `LIMIT_GRAPH_ENABLED=true` |
| `modp`, `cost` | `MODP_ENABLED=true` |
| `rlhf` | `RLHF_ENABLED=true` |
| `distillation`, `training` | `DISTILLATION_ENABLED=true` |
| `evolutionary`, `training` | `EVOLUTIONARY_ENABLED=true` |
| `moe` | `MOE_ENABLED=true` |
| `flexgen`, `energy` | `FLEXGEN_ENABLED=true` |
| `zero_trust`, `safety` | `ZERO_TRUST_ENABLED=true` |
| `privacy` | `DIFFERENTIAL_PRIVACY_ENABLED=true` |
| `checkpoint`, `experiment` | `TRAINING_ENABLED=true` |
| `cache` | always on (lean-ctx core) |
| `digest` | union of all enabled modes |

### Fallback & Error Taxonomy

| Condition | Behavior | Signal |
|-----------|----------|--------|
| Module disabled | Return `{}` (empty result) | `fallback.count` +1 |
| Module file missing | Return `{}` | `fallback.count` +1 |
| Schema version mismatch | Best-effort parse + warning in result | `fallback.schema_warn` |
| Mode unknown to lean-ctx build | Fall through to `full` | `fallback.unknown_mode` |
| Composite sub-mode fails | Return only successful sub-results | `fallback.partial` |
| File unreadable | Standard `ctx_read` error | propagate |

All fallbacks are **non-fatal**. Log line format:

```
[lean-ctx] fallback mode=<mode> reason=<reason> path=<path>
```

### Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| `ctx_read(..., mode="graph")` returns `{}` | `LIMIT_GRAPH_ENABLED` off | enable flag or use `full` |
| Mode returns full file | mode not supported by build | upgrade lean-ctx; check `version` |
| `digest` missing sections | sub-module disabled | enable the missing flag |
| `ctx_edit` repeatedly failing | file has no match / race | re-read via `ctx_read`, then retry once; never loop |
| High token spend | using `full` on large files | switch to enhanced mode |

### Mode Contract & Versioning

- **Contract**: every enhanced mode returns a JSON-serialisable object whose top level matches `schemas/<mode>_vN.json`. Backwards-incompatible changes bump `N`.
- **Version check**: `ctx_read(..., mode="meta")` reports the lean-ctx build and supported modes.
- **Deprecation**: modes are deprecated for **one minor release** before removal; a warning is emitted with the replacement mode name.

### Remember

> Always prefer the **most context-efficient read mode**.
> Use `full` **only** for files you intend to edit.
> Use **enhanced modes** for quick state inspection.
> Use **composite modes** to avoid multiple round-trips.
> Use **`digest`** for a one-shot snapshot of the whole enhancement state.

